Key doc comment on Windows non-support, `RtkService.ts:272`:
```
// No Windows native release exists upstream — manual-install guidance only there.
```
And symlink rationale, `RtkService.ts:137-144` (comment above `getUserPathSymlinkPath`) states explicitly: "Returns null on Windows because no native release exists upstream."

Note: `writeHookSettings()` in `ptyHookSettings.ts:171-177` documents that the rtk hook's curl-based command is POSIX-sh only "by design," since "Dash ships macOS arm64 + Linux x64 only" for rtk — i.e., Windows is not a supported rtk target at all in the hook-writing path either.

